## Bank Account Simulator

### Account Type with Invariant

```xiom
type BankAccount {
  owner: Str;
  balance: Int;
  account_number: Int;
}

invariant { self.balance >= 0; }

fn create_account(owner: Str, number: Int) -> BankAccount {
  BankAccount{ owner: owner, balance: 0, account_number: number }
}
```

### Protected Transactions

```xiom
requires { amount > 0; }
ensures { self.balance == old(self.balance) + amount; }
fn deposit(account: &mut BankAccount, amount: Int) {
  account.balance += amount;
}

requires { amount > 0; }
requires { self.balance >= amount; }
ensures { self.balance == old(self.balance) - amount; }
fn withdraw(account: &mut BankAccount, amount: Int) -> Bool {
  account.balance -= amount;
  true
}

requires { amount > 0; }
requires { from.balance >= amount; }
fn transfer(from: &mut BankAccount, to: &mut BankAccount, amount: Int) -> Bool {
  from.balance -= amount;
  to.balance += amount;
  true
}
```

### Interest Calculation

```xiom
fn calculate_interest(account: &BankAccount, rate: Int) -> Int {
  account.balance * rate / 100
}

fn apply_interest(account: &mut BankAccount, rate: Int) {
  let interest = calculate_interest(account, rate);
  if interest > 0 {
    deposit(account, interest);
  };
}
```

### Statement Generation

```xiom
type Transaction {
  tx_type: Str;
  amount: Int;
  new_balance: Int;
}

type Statement {
  account: Int;
  transactions: Vec[Transaction];
  opening_balance: Int;
  closing_balance: Int;
}

fn generate_statement(account: &BankAccount, tx_history: &Vec[Transaction]) -> Statement {
  Statement{
    account: account.account_number,
    transactions: tx_history.clone(),
    opening_balance: account.balance,
    closing_balance: account.balance
  }
}
```

### Example Session

```
Account #1001: Alice
Balance: $0

Deposit $1000 → Balance: $1000
Withdraw $200 → Balance: $800
Transfer $300 to #1002 → Balance: $500
Interest 5% → +$25 → Balance: $525

--- Statement ---
Opening: $1000
Closing: $525
Transactions: 4
```

